xsd: build the bundled libxsd-frontend with libc++ 19.

The build passes -I libxsd-frontend, which holds a plain-text file named
version. libc++ <limits> includes <version>, so the compiler read
"2.0.0" as C++ and every xsd source failed. post-patch already removes
version files for this reason, but at paths that do not exist in the
+dep source layout. Nothing reads libxsd-frontend/version.

With the file gone, two libc++ 19 removals remain: the generic
std::char_traits (types.hxx, fix based on FreeBSD ports c1c4aae6) and
the public __wrap_iter::base() (state-processor.cxx).
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted); upstream status: not submitted.

--- a/devel/xsd/Makefile
+++ b/devel/xsd/Makefile
@@ -29,6 +29,8 @@
 	# Avoid conflict with C++20 <version>
 	${RM} -f ${WRKSRC}/version
 	${RM} -f ${WRKSRC}/build/import/lib*/version
+	# libxsd-frontend is on the include path; its version file is not read.
+	${RM} -f ${WRKSRC}/libxsd-frontend/version
 
 .include "../../devel/libcutl/buildlink3.mk"
 .include "../../textproc/xerces-c/buildlink3.mk"
